families_seen_among_failures:
  - id: private_fn_visibility
    count: 633
    shape: "error: semantic: private fn `<fn>` of module `<mod>`" — unit specs importing
      module-private fns; ~25 distinct module::fn pairs, one missing export blocking
      11-25 specs each.
    fixed:
      - modules: [test.fixtures.structural.profile_golden_v1,
                  test.fixtures.spipe_controlled_work.controlled_work_proof,
                  test.fixtures.interpreter_global_array_push_linear.shapes]
        commit: af0e67b749ce6
        rescued: 25 of 43 affected specs green (residue fails on unrelated causes)
      - modules: [compiler.loader.smf_cache_manager]
        commit: 38a5a61374704
        rescued: 14 of 18 affected specs green (residue: mir_opt private-fn imports, 2 assertion fails)
    routed: 572 specs as SKIP/owner-decision (ledger cause names module+fn); top
      modules: compiler.backend.native.isel_x86_64 (25), gpu_portable_compute (25),
      riscv_target (24), encode_x86_64 (24), native.mod (23), rules_clib_parity (23),
      gpu_generated_2d_contract (23), backend_helpers (23), app.ui.tui.event_wait (22),
      app.ui.ipc.async_handler (22). Widening compiler/app-internal visibility needs
      owner sign-off; recommended pattern = the two fix commits above (visibility only).
  - id: cannot_resolve_module
    count: "~60 at last scan"
    shape: "error: semantic: Cannot resolve module: <mod>" — moved/renamed modules
      (e.g. app.t32_cli.commands). Unfixed at commit time.
  - id: runner_300s_timeouts
    count: 145+ observed (growing)
    shape: "error: timeout: execution exceeded 300 second limit" — heavy specs
      (app/cli native-build invocations cluster). Class: TIMEOUT-skip per task rules.
  - id: batch_cap_timeouts
    count: ~300 at last scan
    shape: 25-spec batch exceeded the 420s external cap — attribution lost for the
      batch; all members marked TIMEOUT, fix-loop re-runs them solo/mini-batch.
  - id: assertion_failures
    count: 1205
    shape: "spec failure: N of M example(s) failed" — real example failures; each
      needs individual triage (not batch-fixable).

warmup_fixes_landed_before_run:
  - commit 4e243764f6be test(level_detection): pin 04_smoke classification to
    TEST_LEVEL_SMOKE — spec predated the SMOKE level; impl doc lists which trees
    stay unclassified (04_smoke not among them). Repaired spec now 20/20.
  - commit 6f57d6aa86d2 chore(vacuous-baseline): drop hir_types_spec stale
    zero-assertion entry — the 2026-11-06 HIR port added real assertions; the
    baseline line stayed. Repaired spec now 8/8.

runner_health_notes:
  - seed emits no MC/DC probes: every spec reports "MC/DC: DEGRADED evidence=absent"
    but its real pass/fail is unaffected (runner is explicit about this).
  - "test --list <spec>" under the seed does NOT enumerate — it silently executes
    the spec (exit 0). Equivalent discovery = filesystem enumeration of *_spec.spl
    (what this lane's harness uses). Phase 2 will re-check.

phase2: not-started at this commit (2h cap consumed by Phase-1 fleet); the
  testrunner-surface specs are being exercised by the Phase-1 run itself and their
  ledger rows will seed Phase 2's clean-cache verification.

process:
  - 16-way round-robin batch workers (25 spec files per invocation, 420s external
    cap, SIMPLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300), per-spec verdict attribution from
    "SPEC FILE VERDICT:" lines; per-spec wall = batch wall / batch size.
  - fix loop: mini-batches of 3 (950s cap), solo-split on cap hit; hard rule kept —
    a spec is never re-run unchanged more than 3 times.
